30846	30957	30833	30833	Tito	310	“ I remember with particular vividness a hastily snatched visit to Athens . Our hurry , and the double danger of being seized as prisoners by the Turks , and of our galley raising anchor before we could return , made it seem like a fevered vision of the night — the wide plain , the girdling mountains , the ruined porticos and columns , either standing far aloof , as if receding from our hurried footsteps , or else jammed in confusedly among the dwellings of Christians degraded into servitude , or among the forts and turrets of their Moslem conquerors , who have their stronghold on the Acropolis . ”
